 "design": "The matched-N LOW- versus HIGH-coverage render experiment: does acquisition-space coverage, at the same number of\ntraining frames, change what a render-only detector does on obliques, on a real spin and on real spot frames?\n\nTHE THREE ARMS, per device card D (surgio_b51_dr first, elekta_xvi second; cios_fusion has no card in the unseen\nangle sweep and is deferred), N matched to the frame count of the existing styled corpus of that device:\n  low     N styled frames whose poses are the device's REAL pool (devcorpus/styled/D__D: AP + lateral for Surgio,\n          H*_lat 0.20 in COVERAGE.md; the COBRA gantry sweep for Elekta, H*_lat 0.86) -- the corpus that exists.\n  high    N styled frames whose poses are drawn from the device's ARC pool ONLY (devcorpus_arc/poses/D.json, the\n          `arc` entries: lat uniform in -90..+90, tilt +-15, roll +-10 about the real AP anchors; H*_lat about 0.95),\n          rendered into devcorpus/render/D_arc and styled by the SAME card into devcorpus/styled/D_arc__D.\n  low2n   the low frames plus N more from the real pool rendered with another seed (devcorpus/render/D_low2): does\n          twice the count of the same bins do what the arc does?\nSame subjects (~/model_night/ts_clean_subjects.txt minus the 40 unseen-sweep subjects, checked disjoint), same card,\nsame draws, same trainer (tools/devcorpus_train.py's YOLO call: COCO yolo11m, 40 epochs, 1024 px, batch 8, the same\naugmentation), same selection frames (the union of the three corpora's val images: the 17 val subjects every devcorpus\narm selected on), seeds 0 and 1. No real frame is trained on.\n\nSCORING, every arm through the same evaluators (each runs tools/eval_gate.py before it scores):\n  (i)   the unseen angle sweep: tools/arc_recall_eval.py on devcorpus_arc/anglesweep_unseen (40 subjects no arm's\n        chain ever saw; recall per 10-deg lat bin, subject-clustered intervals);\n  (ii)  the real case134 CBCT spin: tools/case134_sweep.py score (one patient, no interval);\n  (iii) the real test frames: tools/realxray_eval.py on every real device's test split via devcorpus_train.score,\n        with the C-ArmLSpine matched-convention (vertebral body) re-score.\n\n",
